<section class="section" id="process">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="task-section-copy"><p class="eyebrow">From sample to batch</p><h2>Agree the fit before repeating the part.</h2><p>The material and print settings depend on how the component will be used. Tell us about load, heat, moisture, chemicals, sunlight, friction and appearance.</p></div>
    <ol class="task-process">
      <li><h3>Describe the problem</h3><p>Share photos, what failed, the equipment involved and the quantity needed. We review feasibility and discuss a likely cost range.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Measure and model</h3><p>We agree the reference dimensions and design scope. CAD views or drawings let you review the proposed geometry.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Check a sample</h3><p>A prototype or a small test section can check difficult features. Where the mating assembly is available, we can check fit here; otherwise you assess the sample.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Approve production</h3><p>For a batch, confirm the sample, material and required checks before the run. Quantity, finishing and delivery are included in the production discussion.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="task-batch-note"><h3>Need the same part repeatedly?</h3><p>Tell us your initial quantity and likely repeat requirement. Developing a replacement once can support later batches; the practical quantity and price depend on the part and agreed specification. <a href="{{ '/services/batch-production/' | url }}">Explore batch production</a>.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
